{"name":"Winter Harbor","hex":"#5e737d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Winter Harbor","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A town on the Schoodic Peninsula, Hancock County, Maine, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Winter_Harbor"}],"entries":[{"title":"Winter Harbor, Maine","blocks":[{"text":"Winter Harbor is a town on the Schoodic Peninsula in Hancock County, Maine, United States. The population was 461 at the 2020 census. The town is located just outside the Schoodic Peninsula portion of Acadia National Park and is due east of the town of Bar Harbor and Ellsworth. Winter Harbor was once the location of a US Naval Station, NSGA-WH, which closed in the mid-2000s, and is now home to the Schoodic Institute’s Education and Research Center."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Aerial_View_Winter_Harbor%2C_Maine.jpg/330px-Aerial_View_Winter_Harbor%2C_Maine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winter_Harbor%2C_Maine","wikidata":"Q3448810"},{"title":"Winter","blocks":[{"text":"Winter is the coldest and darkest season of the year in temperate and polar climates. It occurs after autumn and before spring, when the hemisphere is oriented away from the Sun as a result of the tilt of Earth's axis. Different cultures define different dates as the start of winter, and some use a definition based on weather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Winter_forest_silver.jpg/330px-Winter_forest_silver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winter","wikidata":"Q1311"},{"title":"Harbor","blocks":[{"text":"A harbor or harbour is a sheltered part of a body of water where ships, boats, and barges can be moored."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Jebel_Ali_Port_2_Imresolt.jpg/330px-Jeb